Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.

The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.

Task 1: Hardening | Disable Swap
Description Task 1: Disable swap on the system, including disabling it temporarily and permanently, when swap is enabled and the vault_hardening_disable_swap variable is set to true.

Task 2: Hardening | Disable Core Dumps
Description Task 2: Disable core dumps for both hard and soft limits, using the community.general.pam_limits module, when the vault_hardening_disable_core_dumps variable is set to true. This involves looping over two items that set the limit to 0.

Task 3: Hardening | Disable Shell Command History
Description Task 3: Disable shell command history by copying the vault.sh file to /etc/profile.d/, when the vault_hardening_disable_shell_command_history variable is set to true. The file includes an export command to ignore certain history entries.

Task 4: Hardening | Configure SELinux / AppArmor
Description Task 4: Configure SELinux and AppArmor, including enabling SELinux when it's already enabled, and enforcing AppArmor. This involves installing the selinux-policy package, setting the SELinux policy to targeted and state to enforcing, and enforcing AppArmor by running the aa-enforce command.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- name: Hardening | Disable Swap
  block:
    - name: Disable swap when enabled and vault_hardening_disable_swap is true
      swapoff:
        state: absent
      when: vault_hardening_disable_swap
    - name: Disable swap at boot
      sysctl:
        name: vm.swappiness
        value: 0
      when: vault_hardening_disable_swap

- name: Hardening | Disable Core Dumps
  when: vault_hardening_disable_core_dumps
  pam_limits:
    - name: core
      value: 0
    - name: coredump_size
      value: 0

- name: Hardening | Disable Shell Command History
  when: vault_hardening_disable_shell_command_history
  copy:
    content: |
      export HISTIGNORE="cd *,ls *,pwd *,clear *,exit *,alias *,unalias *,export *,source *,set *,unset *,env *,printenv *,declare *,typeset *,function *,enable *,disable *,bind *,bindkey *,keymap *,keybind *,bindfile *,bindkeyfile *,bindkeymap *,bindkeyfilemap *,bindkeyfile *
      export PROMPT_COMMAND='', PS1='', PROMPT=' ', PS1=' ', HISTTIMEFORMAT='', PROMPT=' ', PS1=' '
    dest: /etc/profile.d/vault.sh
    mode: '0644'

- name: Hardening | Configure SELinux / AppArmor
  block:
    - name: Install selinux-policy package
      package:
        name: selinux-policy
        state: present

    - name: Enable SELinux when already enabled
      selinux:
        policy: targeted
        state: enabled

    - name: Enforce AppArmor
      shell: aa-enforce


